WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:13.250
83. Johann Sebastian Bach. Johann Sebastian Bach, 1685 to 1750, was one of the most important

2
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:20.290
composers in the history of music. When we think of classical music, his name is one of the first

3
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:27.850
to come up. He was not necessarily an innovator. Instead, his talent was to express the musical

4
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:36.010
style of his age in the most complete and mature way. Bach grew up in the era of Baroque music. He

5
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:42.650
learned to play a variety of instruments as a child, and he was also an excellent singer. During his

6
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:48.970
life, he was better known as a musician than a composer. But now we remember him for the

7
00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:57.290
compositions he left behind. Bach's music is special for several reasons. First of all, Bach was a

8
00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:03.610
fantastic craftsman. During his life, he was employed to create different types of music

9
00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:10.650
for different people. This required him to explore different types of music and different sounds and

10
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:17.290
broaden his own musical style. Perhaps because of this experience, he would add foreign musical

11
00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:24.810
influences to his own compositions. Bach also valued completeness. In many of his compositions,

12
00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:32.490
a single musical idea is explored fully. This might mean playing a melody in every possible key

13
00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:39.690
or at many different speeds. Bach's works often seem to approach one musical idea from many angles.

14
00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:46.890
He was a master of counterpoint. Counterpoint is when two voices sing two very different patterns

15
00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:54.170
of music that somehow blend together in harmony. He was able to make two distinct lines of music

16
00:01:54.170 --> 00:02:01.210
complete each other. Finally, Bach created feeling in his compositions. Particularly with

17
00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:09.050
his religious music, Bach was able to make listeners truly feel his passion. Bach's detailed,

18
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:16.570
controlled compositions are seen as the height of Baroque music. His passion and dedication ensured

19
00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:20.810
that his name remains alive hundreds of years after his death.
